load @term/seed/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# A quadratic form: a homogeneous degree-two polynomial on a vector space, a sum of squares and cross terms, the machine
# that assigns a number to each vector and from which a Clifford algebra is built (a vector squares to its quadratic
# form value). Its signature (how many plus and minus squares) classifies it, and the positive-definite forms are the
# inner products. The norm of each rung of the number tower is a quadratic form. The form carries the underlying vector
# space; the degree-two homogeneity is the defining shape.
form quadratic-form
  link space, like vector-space
